@startuml E3-deployment-02-wallet-trading-mvc
title CryptoWeb - Deployment 02: Wallet and Market Trading (MVC)

!theme plain
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 110
skinparam ranksep 120
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "Client browser" as Browser {
  artifact "Wallet / Trades views" as UI
    artifact "walletApi.js + tradeApi.js" as ClientAPI
}
node "Server_3 Node.js :4000" as S3 {
  artifact "trade/wallet controllers" as S3Ctrl
  artifact "personA.gateway.js" as Gateway
  artifact "MongoDB Trade model" as TradeModel
}
node "Core Node.js :5000" as Core {
  artifact "trade / wallet controllers" as CoreCtrl
  artifact "settlement service modules" as Trading
  artifact "SQL wallet / holding data access" as Wallet
}
database "Core MySQL\nwallets / transactions / holdings / fills" as SQL
database "Server_3 MongoDB\ntrades (history projection)" as Mongo
cloud "Binance price API" as Binance

Browser --> S3 : BUY / SELL wallet mutation 
Browser --> Core : balance / history admin adjustment
S3 --> Core : trade execute / wallet proxy REST + service credentials
Core --> SQL : atomic settlement
Core --> Binance : market-price retrieval
S3 --> Mongo : synchronize executed fill

note bottom of SQL
  Core commits wallet updates, holdings,
  wallet transaction CONFIRMED and fill FILLED.
  Ledger recording is a separate operation.
end note
note bottom of S3
  MVC view: React Views use API clients; controllers use actual service/model modules.
end note

@enduml
